# FILE: .gitignore
# WHAT IT DOES: Keeps local secrets, build output, caches, and editor files out of Git.
# ROLE IN THE PROJECT: Prevents credentials and generated files from being committed.
# IF YOU REMOVE THIS FILE: .env, node_modules, .next, and target can appear in Git status.
# DEPENDS ON: Git ignore rules.
# USED BY: Git.
# KEY FUNCTIONS: None; each line names an ignored path pattern.

.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.next/
node_modules/
out/
coverage/
target/
.mvn/wrapper/dists/
.mvn/wrapper/maven-wrapper.jar
.idea/
.vscode/
*.log
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store
